# Security review: no findings

No high-confidence vulnerability in setup:deps:kotlin, setup:deps:swift,
setup:deps:android or code:lint:android.

Candidates examined and excluded:
- `eval "FILES=(${usage_files})"` (tools/android/.config/mise/tasks/code/lint/android:60): the same line exists on the base branch in code:lint/code:format dispatchers and the dart tasks; file names come from the developer's own repository, which then runs its own ./gradlew. No new attack surface.
- Gradle checksum check (tools/kotlin/.config/mise/tasks/setup/deps/kotlin ~:31): checks only the format of distributionSha256Sum; wrapper and distributionUrl come from the same repository. Hygiene, not a defence; a bypass gains nothing.
- Lockfile backup and restore (kotlin): paths from git ls-files, relative to the root; backup in mktemp -d; deletes only lockfiles in the repository and its own temp folder. No path traversal.
- Package.resolved backup (swift): mktemp; the trap restores to a fixed path in the repository.
- SDK package ids (android): levels from build files must match ^[0-9]+(\.[0-9]+)?$; EMULATOR_IMAGE and COMPILE_SDK are trusted env values; every value is quoted for android sdk install.
No script writes credentials to its output.
